    "content": "# Cookie Policy\n\n**Last updated: March 22, 2026**\n\nThis Cookie Policy explains how SERP (\"we,\" \"us,\" or \"our\") uses cookies and similar tracking technologies when you visit our website (serp.co) and related services.\n\n## 1. What Are Cookies\n\nCookies are small text files that are stored on your device (computer, tablet, or mobile) when you visit a website. They are widely used to make websites work more efficiently and to provide information to website owners.\n\n### 1.1 Types of Cookies We Use\n\n- **Session Cookies**: Temporary cookies that are deleted when you close your browser\n- **Persistent Cookies**: Cookies that remain on your device for a set period or until you delete them\n- **First-Party Cookies**: Cookies set by our website directly\n- **Third-Party Cookies**: Cookies set by external services we use\n\n## 2. How We Use Cookies\n\n### 2.1 Essential Cookies\n\nThese cookies are necessary for the website to function properly and cannot be disabled:\n\n| Cookie Name | Purpose | Duration | Type |\n| ----------- | ------- | -------- | ---- |\n| `__clerk_*` | Authentication and session management | Session/30 days | Essential |\n\n### 2.2 Analytics Cookies\n\nWe use privacy-focused analytics to understand how visitors use our website:\n\n| Service | Purpose | Data Processing | Opt-Out |\n| ------- | ------- | --------------- | ------- |\n| OpenPanel | Product analytics | Cookieless, no personal data | Browser settings |\n\n**Note**: OpenPanel is privacy-focused and does not use tracking cookies or collect personal data.\n\n### 2.3 Local Storage (Not Cookies)\n\nWe use browser local storage (not cookies) to enhance your experience:\n\n| Storage Key | Purpose | Duration | Type |\n| ----------- | ------- | -------- | ---- |\n| `llms-hub-favorites` | Store your favorite websites locally | Until manually cleared | Local Storage |\n| `websites-show-all` | Remember show all preference | Until manually cleared | Local Storage |\n| `websites-sort-by` | Remember sort preferences | Until manually cleared | Local Storage |\n| `category-sort-by` | Remember category sort preferences | Until manually cleared | Local Storage |\n| `recentSearches` | Store recent search history | Until manually cleared | Local Storage |\n\n**Note**: Local storage data stays on your device and is not sent to our servers. This data persists until you clear your browser data or uninstall the browser.\n\n## 3. Cookie Consent\n\n### 3.1 Essential Cookies\nEssential cookies are automatically enabled as they are necessary for the website to function. These include:\n- Authentication and security cookies\n- Basic functionality cookies\n- User preference cookies\n\n### 3.2 Non-Essential Cookies\nFor non-essential cookies, we:\n- Provide clear information about their purpose\n- Seek your consent before setting them\n- Allow you to withdraw consent at any time\n- Respect browser \"Do Not Track\" signals where applicable\n\n## 4. Managing Your Cookie Preferences\n\n### 4.1 Browser Settings\n\nYou can control cookies through your browser settings:\n\n- **Chrome**: Settings > Privacy and Security > Cookies and other site data\n- **Firefox**: Settings > Privacy & Security > Cookies and Site Data\n- **Safari**: Preferences > Privacy > Cookies and website data\n- **Edge**: Settings > Privacy, search, and services > Cookies and site permissions\n\n### 4.2 Cookie Categories\n\n- **Strictly Necessary**: Cannot be disabled as they are essential for website functionality\n- **Analytics**: Can be disabled; will not affect website functionality\n- **Functional**: Can be disabled; may affect some website features\n\n### 4.3 Impact of Disabling Cookies\n\n| Cookie Type | Impact if Disabled |\n| ----------- | ------------------ |\n| Essential (`__clerk_*`) | Cannot log in or maintain sessions |\n| Analytics | No impact on functionality |\n\n### 4.4 Impact of Clearing Local Storage\n\n| Storage Type | Impact if Cleared |\n| ------------ | ----------------- |\n| Favorites | Will lose all saved favorite websites |\n| Sort/Filter Preferences | Will reset to default sort and filter settings |\n| Recent Searches | Will lose search history and autocomplete suggestions |\n\n## 5. Third-Party Services\n\n### 5.1 Authentication (Clerk)\n- **Purpose**: User authentication and account management\n- **Cookies Set**: Session and authentication tokens\n- **Data Processing**: User profile and authentication data\n- **Privacy Policy**: [Clerk Privacy Policy](https://clerk.com/privacy)\n\n### 5.2 Analytics (OpenPanel)\n- **Purpose**: Product analytics and user behavior insights\n- **Cookies Set**: None (cookieless tracking)\n- **Data Processing**: Anonymized usage statistics only\n- **Privacy Policy**: [OpenPanel Privacy Policy](https://openpanel.dev/privacy)\n\n### 5.3 Hosting (Vercel)\n- **Purpose**: Website hosting and performance\n- **Cookies Set**: Performance and security cookies\n- **Data Processing**: Technical logs and performance data\n- **Privacy Policy**: [Vercel Privacy Policy](https://vercel.com/privacy)\n\n## 6. International Cookie Laws\n\n### 6.1 European Union (GDPR)\nUnder EU law, we:\n- Obtain consent before setting non-essential cookies\n- Provide clear information about cookie purposes\n- Allow easy withdrawal of consent\n- Ensure cookies are necessary and proportionate\n\n### 6.2 United Kingdom (UK GDPR & PECR)\nWe comply with UK cookie regulations by:\n- Following the same principles as EU GDPR\n- Respecting the ICO's cookie guidance\n- Providing appropriate consent mechanisms\n\n### 6.3 California (CCPA)\nFor California residents:\n- Cookies may constitute \"personal information\" under CCPA\n- You have rights regarding cookie-based data collection\n- See our Privacy Policy for California-specific rights\n\n## 7. Cookie Security\n\n### 7.1 Security Measures\nWe implement security measures for cookies:\n- Secure flag for HTTPS-only cookies\n- HttpOnly flag to prevent JavaScript access (where appropriate)\n- SameSite attribute to prevent CSRF attacks\n- Regular security reviews and updates\n\n### 7.2 Data Protection\n- Cookies containing personal data are encrypted\n- Authentication cookies have short expiration times\n- We regularly audit cookie usage and purposes\n\n## 8. Changes to This Cookie Policy\n\n### 8.1 Updates\nWe may update this Cookie Policy to:\n- Reflect changes in our cookie usage\n- Comply with legal requirements\n- Improve clarity and transparency\n\n### 8.2 Notification\nWhen we make significant changes:\n- We will update the \"Last updated\" date\n- We may notify you via email or website banner\n- Continued use indicates acceptance of changes\n\n## 9. Contact Us\n\nFor questions about our cookie usage:\n\n**Email**: [privacy@serp.co](mailto:privacy@serp.co)\n**Subject Line**: Cookie Policy Inquiry\n**Response Time**: Within 30 days\n\nFor technical issues with cookies:\n**Email**: [support@serp.co](mailto:support@serp.co)\n\n## 10. Additional Resources\n\n### 10.1 Learn More About Cookies\n- [All About Cookies](https://www.allaboutcookies.org/)\n- [Your Online Choices](http://www.youronlinechoices.eu/)\n- [Network Advertising Initiative](http://www.networkadvertising.org/)\n\n### 10.2 Browser Cookie Information\n- [Google Chrome Cookie Settings](https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647)\n- [Mozilla Firefox Cookie Settings](https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/enhanced-tracking-protection-firefox-desktop)\n- [Apple Safari Cookie Settings](https://support.apple.com/en-us/105082)\n- [Microsoft Edge Cookie Settings](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09)\n\n---\n\n**Effective Date**: March 22, 2026\n\nThis Cookie Policy is effective as of March 22, 2026, and was last updated on March 22, 2026.",
