    "content": "# JSON Shapes\n\n<p className=\"mt-2 text-xl text-muted-foreground\">The active starter uses local data first. The main source of truth is `data/websites.json`, while docs and guides still come from MDX content files.</p>\n\n## `data/websites.json`\n\nThis file is an array of website entries.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"slug\": \"example-project-llms-txt\",\n    \"name\": \"Example Project\",\n    \"website\": \"https://example.com\",\n    \"description\": \"Short summary of the project and its docs.\",\n    \"llmsUrl\": \"https://example.com/llms.txt\",\n    \"llmsFullUrl\": \"https://example.com/llms-full.txt\",\n    \"category\": \"developer-tools\",\n    \"favicon\": \"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=example.com&sz=128\",\n    \"featured\": true,\n    \"publishedAt\": \"2026-03-22\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n### Website entry fields\n\n| Field | Required | Notes |\n|------|------|------|\n| `slug` | Recommended | Stable URL segment for `/websites/[slug]`. The loader can derive it from `name` if it is missing. |\n| `name` | Yes | Display name used in cards, search, and detail pages. |\n| `website` | Yes | Canonical site URL. The loader also accepts the legacy `domain` field. |\n| `description` | Yes | Plain text summary. The loader strips HTML if older content included markup. |\n| `llmsUrl` | Yes | Primary `llms.txt` URL. The loader also accepts the legacy `llmsTxtUrl` alias. |\n| `llmsFullUrl` | No | Optional `llms-full.txt` URL. |\n| `category` | Yes | Category slug used by the starter UI. |\n| `featured` | No | Marks the entry for featured lists. |\n| `favicon` | No | Generated convenience field. The current UI does not require it to render. |\n| `publishedAt` | Yes | Date string used for sorting and “recently added” sections. |\n\n## Loader compatibility rules\n\nThe website loader currently accepts a few migration-friendly variations:\n\n- `website` or `domain`\n- `llmsUrl` or `llmsTxtUrl`\n- Missing `slug`, as long as `name` is present\n\nThe loader also:\n\n- Sanitizes descriptions into plain text\n- Sorts entries by `publishedAt`, newest first\n- Maps the JSON entry into the active `WebsiteMetadata` shape used by the app\n\n## Recommended category slugs\n\nUse the same category slugs that the active app understands:\n\n- `ai-ml`\n- `developer-tools`\n- `data-analytics`\n- `automation-workflow`\n- `infrastructure-cloud`\n- `security-identity`\n\nDuring the current migration, some older local content may still contain legacy automation slugs. Prefer `automation-workflow` for new entries.\n\n## Submit form payload shape\n\nThe `/submit` form does not write JSON directly. It builds a GitHub issue URL from this client-side shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Example Project\",\n  \"website\": \"https://example.com\",\n  \"llmsUrl\": \"https://example.com/llms.txt\",\n  \"llmsFullUrl\": \"https://example.com/llms-full.txt\",\n  \"category\": \"developer-tools\",\n  \"description\": \"Short summary of the project.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Optional reviewer context.\"\n}\n```\n\nThat payload is converted into a prefilled GitHub issue. See [Submit Workflow](/docs/submit-workflow) for the full handoff.\n\n## Other content shapes\n\nThe starter is JSON-first for the directory, but docs and guides still use MDX frontmatter.\n\n### Docs frontmatter\n\n```md\n---\ntitle: 'Page title'\ndescription: 'Short summary'\norder: 1\npublished: true\n---\n```\n\n### Guides frontmatter\n\n```md\n---\ntitle: 'Guide title'\ndescription: 'Short summary'\ndate: '2026-03-22'\nimage: '/guides/example.webp'\nauthors:\n  - name: 'Your Name'\ndifficulty: 'beginner'\ncategory: 'getting-started'\npublished: true\n---\n```",
