    "content": "# Submit Workflow\n\n<p className=\"mt-2 text-xl text-muted-foreground\">The active starter keeps submissions simple. The site gathers the basics, then sends the user to a prefilled GitHub issue for review.</p>\n\n## Why the starter uses GitHub issues\n\nThe current starter does not run a submissions backend. It stays static-friendly by using GitHub as the review queue.\n\nThat means the active app does not need:\n\n- Site auth\n- A database\n- A server action or API route for submissions\n- A moderation dashboard in the app itself\n\nInstead, the repo becomes the source of truth and GitHub becomes the audit trail.\n\n## What happens when someone submits\n\n1. The user opens `/submit`.\n2. The form collects the project name, category, website URL, and any optional notes.\n3. When the website field loses focus, the form suggests `llms.txt` and `llms-full.txt` URLs from the same origin.\n4. When the user clicks **Continue on GitHub**, the client builds a GitHub issue URL.\n5. The browser navigates to the GitHub issue composer with a template, title, and prefilled body.\n6. A maintainer reviews the issue and, if approved, updates repo data such as `data/websites.json` or the website content files.\n\n## Example GitHub issue URL\n\n```txt\nhttps://github.com/thedaviddias/llms-txt-hub/issues/new\n  ?template=submit-website.yml\n  &title=Submit llms.txt: Example Project\n  &body=...\n```\n\n## Example prefilled issue body\n\n```md\n## Website details\n\nName: Example Project\nWebsite: https://example.com\nllms.txt URL: https://example.com/llms.txt\nCategory: developer-tools\n\n## Description\n\nA short summary of what the project does and why its llms.txt is useful.\n\n## Additional notes\n\nOptional reviewer context.\n```\n\n## Files that control the flow\n\n- `apps/web/app/submit/page.tsx` renders the public submit page.\n- `apps/web/components/forms/github-issue-submit-form.tsx` renders the form and handles the client-side redirect.\n- `apps/web/components/forms/submit-form-utils.ts` suggests `llms.txt` and `llms-full.txt` URLs from the website origin.\n- `apps/web/lib/github-issue.ts` builds the final GitHub issue URL, template, title, and body.\n\n## What to change if you customize it\n\n- Change the GitHub owner, repo, or template in `apps/web/lib/github-issue.ts`.\n- Add or remove fields in `apps/web/components/forms/github-issue-submit-form.tsx`.\n- Keep the GitHub issue handoff if you want to stay static-friendly with no runtime infrastructure.\n\nIf you also need the active data contract for accepted entries, see [JSON Shapes](/docs/json-shapes).",
